{"assessments":[{"definition":{"content":"{\n  \"id\": \"AR-046\",\n  \"type\": \"allocated-requirement\",\n  \"title\": \"Preserve meaning and attribution across browser views\",\n  \"status\": \"draft\",\n  \"statement\": \"The Views and traceability Module shall preserve meaning and attribution across browser views within its accountable browser contribution to SR-085, retaining the stated limits of collaborating owners.\",\n  \"analysis\": {\n    \"method\": \"5W2H\",\n    \"what\": {\n      \"problem\": \"A locally successful browser step can hide missing ownership or an invalid cross-boundary conclusion.\",\n      \"desired_outcome\": \"Preserve meaning and attribution across browser views.\"\n    },\n    \"why\": {\n      \"rationale\": \"MOD-004 owns the behavior necessary for the selected SR-085 criteria; the SR remains the system-wide obligation.\"\n    },\n    \"who\": {\n      \"stakeholders\": [\n        \"Customer authors and readers\",\n        \"Product maintainers and reviewers\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"when\": {\n      \"conditions\": [\n        \"When generating, reading, recovering or qualifying the selected browser scope.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"where\": {\n      \"contexts\": [\n        \"MOD-004 and its declared browser cooperation contracts.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"how\": {\n      \"approach\": \"Apply the constrained Functions and preserve source, output, qualification and authority distinctions at the boundary.\"\n    },\n    \"how_much\": {\n      \"scope\": \"Contribution to SR-085 criteria 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6. Other Module contributions and final product qualification remain distinct.\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n    \"Readers can navigate each available view from an overview to relevant definitions, relationships and applicable rationale, using readable labels and keyboard-accessible navigation.\",\n    \"Logical ownership and containment remain distinct from execution and deployment; a shared source file does not merge logical responsibilities.\",\n    \"Process topology does not imply execution order or concurrency. Selected activity, interaction and lifecycle details appear only where authoritative semantics establish them.\",\n    \"Proposed and observed facts remain distinguishable in overviews and details, even when names are identical; each detail exposes its selected-state source basis.\",\n    \"Scenario navigation retains stakeholder meaning and identified architecture participation without turning reachability or rendering into coverage, approval or satisfaction.\",\n    \"Missing required explanation and incomplete selections remain explicit; absent details are not fabricated and view success does not establish a complete design.\"\n  ],\n  \"assumptions\": [],\n  \"constraints\": [\n    \"Draft allocation; does not establish implemented browser support or requirement satisfaction.\"\n  ],\n  \"allocated_to\": \"MOD-004\",\n  \"constrains\": [\n    \"FUNC-007\",\n    \"FUNC-009\",\n    \"FUNC-080\",\n    \"FUNC-081\"\n  ],\n  \"sources\": [\n    {\n      \"source\": \"SRC-CUSTOMER-BROWSER-DESIGN\",\n      \"locator\": \"AR-046; SR-085 criteria 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6\",\n      \"basis\": \"System and Architecture Design from SR-084–088 and refined SR-060; proposed responsibility, contract and realization only. No implementation, platform qualification or product availability is established.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n","identity":"sha256:1dee4e8814f45c1943675afcd28d2facd53586f7e18bb85d9d7caca8b269233f","path":"design/requirements/IR-002-trace-engineering-obligations-and-responsibilities/SR-085-preserve-engineering-meaning-across-architecture-views/AR-046-preserve-meaning-and-attribution-across-browser-views.json"},"implementation":{"actor":"root / verify (implementation-source assessment)","applicability":{"explanation":"Exact material sources inspected and compared. Actual assessor scope, observations and residual customer-context gaps retained; no full-scope positive conclusion.","state":"current"},"child_support":[],"concerns":[],"criteria":[{"evidence":[{"limitations":["Accountable source inspection of repository implementation; check names below identify relevant assertions, not an automatic full-criterion pass."],"source":{"change":"2026-10-04-system-requirements-view-design","id":"criterion-assessment-implementation","identity":"sha256:f4223bb2644ad82b0ae43bf7dc6938d5c87604cddcd93fbc49b6e4cbb8b7b65e","kind":"evidence"},"subjects":[{"identity":"sha256:5c7447a3241ef95ea4c3e8444517006e1faf4b30e0306cace0803b5165725932","path":"scripts/lib/rem_architecture_browser.py"},{"identity":"sha256:8d5e4e7cee2dd6280d2127fe86442e1d43f83d9fb7826e902d30a7bc4e890cfa","path":"scripts/lib/rem_architecture_model.py"},{"identity":"sha256:88ccf64b75ac66b2ca6a64a6711667b724fb5a5a31f699d97760712f076ab964","path":"scripts/lib/rem_authored_views.py"},{"identity":"sha256:a0b9939b83431dc400d282973b37beced5e4d932bb74bdbe838e76270732f402","path":"scripts/render-rem-architecture-browser.py"},{"identity":"sha256:fff142393fc3f195ee04860df52f2a300275226a239273ca8e3594e7914806f8","path":"scripts/resources/rem-architecture-browser/viewer.css"},{"identity":"sha256:78e1ed7cfb328736008755d11c044ac318487d6464c3340e5b413eb4f5d0a934","path":"scripts/resources/rem-architecture-browser/viewer.js"},{"identity":"sha256:586ed3d8faea1d8ed6133f9f67d3592594bec6c9d809955a704b22c185a3b9ce","path":"tests/engineering/validation/architecture_browser_tests.py"},{"identity":"sha256:78178721aa41b5967600b8f9848ccbabb157a0588b48da48b0e1919f3e3c7ed3","path":"tests/engineering/validation/architecture_browser_ui_checks.cjs"},{"identity":"sha256:0ca36cdcd69c7204aeb53a1d0f46aeab1fc54dd96f8262883a6f6fa7c2955e86","path":"tests/engineering/validation/architecture_view_tests.py"}],"summary":"The repository renderer embeds source records, typed relationships and qualified topics; the reader links system and Module overviews to definitions, relationships, source text and rationale. Native links, buttons and focus handling support keyboard navigation, including the expandable requirement tree."}],"explanation":"The repository renderer embeds source records, typed relationships and qualified topics; the reader links system and Module overviews to definitions, relationships, source text and rationale. Native links, buttons and focus handling support keyboard navigation, including the expandable requirement tree. This is an observed MOD-004 contribution; collaborating capture/interpretation and package qualification remain separately owned.","gaps":["Demonstrate overview-to-definition/relationship/required-rationale navigation across all available views on the selected customer model, with declared keyboard/readability support and explicit unavailable rationale."],"key":"C1","state":"partial"},{"evidence":[{"limitations":["Accountable source inspection of repository implementation; check names below identify relevant assertions, not an automatic full-criterion pass."],"source":{"change":"2026-10-04-system-requirements-view-design","id":"criterion-assessment-implementation","identity":"sha256:f4223bb2644ad82b0ae43bf7dc6938d5c87604cddcd93fbc49b6e4cbb8b7b65e","kind":"evidence"},"subjects":[{"identity":"sha256:5c7447a3241ef95ea4c3e8444517006e1faf4b30e0306cace0803b5165725932","path":"scripts/lib/rem_architecture_browser.py"},{"identity":"sha256:8d5e4e7cee2dd6280d2127fe86442e1d43f83d9fb7826e902d30a7bc4e890cfa","path":"scripts/lib/rem_architecture_model.py"},{"identity":"sha256:4ef2966248278de32fa8e138c270333df889f7f39bfef80a5232a3aa5cea1740","path":"scripts/lib/rem_architecture_physical.py"},{"identity":"sha256:2ec4643a7735f85cd67b670a34c7aa52e71352ea5c19101e53e0ac5a48358e77","path":"scripts/lib/rem_architecture_realization_diagrams.py"},{"identity":"sha256:78e1ed7cfb328736008755d11c044ac318487d6464c3340e5b413eb4f5d0a934","path":"scripts/resources/rem-architecture-browser/viewer.js"},{"identity":"sha256:586ed3d8faea1d8ed6133f9f67d3592594bec6c9d809955a704b22c185a3b9ce","path":"tests/engineering/validation/architecture_browser_tests.py"},{"identity":"sha256:78178721aa41b5967600b8f9848ccbabb157a0588b48da48b0e1919f3e3c7ed3","path":"tests/engineering/validation/architecture_browser_ui_checks.cjs"},{"identity":"sha256:0ca36cdcd69c7204aeb53a1d0f46aeab1fc54dd96f8262883a6f6fa7c2955e86","path":"tests/engineering/validation/architecture_view_tests.py"}],"summary":"build_model separates direct Function/AR allocation from subtree summaries and exact Interface provider from exposure. Development diagrams group source mappings under each accountable owner; typed execution and placement projections use separate source facts. Shared source paths therefore do not define or merge logical ownership."}],"explanation":"build_model separates direct Function/AR allocation from subtree summaries and exact Interface provider from exposure. Development diagrams group source mappings under each accountable owner; typed execution and placement projections use separate source facts. Shared source paths therefore do not define or merge logical ownership. This is an observed MOD-004 contribution; collaborating capture/interpretation and package qualification remain separately owned.","gaps":["Carry the proven repository shared-source ownership distinction through the admitted customer capture, interpretation, projection and artifact boundary; inspect overview and details with differing runtime/placement facts."],"key":"C2","state":"partial"},{"evidence":[{"limitations":["Accountable source inspection of repository implementation; check names below identify relevant assertions, not an automatic full-criterion pass."],"source":{"change":"2026-10-04-system-requirements-view-design","id":"criterion-assessment-implementation","identity":"sha256:f4223bb2644ad82b0ae43bf7dc6938d5c87604cddcd93fbc49b6e4cbb8b7b65e","kind":"evidence"},"subjects":[{"identity":"sha256:5c7447a3241ef95ea4c3e8444517006e1faf4b30e0306cace0803b5165725932","path":"scripts/lib/rem_architecture_browser.py"},{"identity":"sha256:8d5e4e7cee2dd6280d2127fe86442e1d43f83d9fb7826e902d30a7bc4e890cfa","path":"scripts/lib/rem_architecture_model.py"},{"identity":"sha256:0fdc7b982237c27e107762d5fcbaac855e5b4852dd923b6b7d1ed23f393bb3e5","path":"scripts/lib/rem_architecture_process.py"},{"identity":"sha256:2ec4643a7735f85cd67b670a34c7aa52e71352ea5c19101e53e0ac5a48358e77","path":"scripts/lib/rem_architecture_realization_diagrams.py"},{"identity":"sha256:78e1ed7cfb328736008755d11c044ac318487d6464c3340e5b413eb4f5d0a934","path":"scripts/resources/rem-architecture-browser/viewer.js"},{"identity":"sha256:586ed3d8faea1d8ed6133f9f67d3592594bec6c9d809955a704b22c185a3b9ce","path":"tests/engineering/validation/architecture_browser_tests.py"},{"identity":"sha256:78178721aa41b5967600b8f9848ccbabb157a0588b48da48b0e1919f3e3c7ed3","path":"tests/engineering/validation/architecture_browser_ui_checks.cjs"},{"identity":"sha256:0ca36cdcd69c7204aeb53a1d0f46aeab1fc54dd96f8262883a6f6fa7c2955e86","path":"tests/engineering/validation/architecture_view_tests.py"}],"summary":"Process validation admits explicit participants, steps, alternatives and guarded lifecycle transitions. Projection separates typed topology from selected sequence/state details; omitted semantic facts are not guessed from prose, software paths or Scenario reachability. The reader labels the selected source meaning and its execution limits."}],"explanation":"Process validation admits explicit participants, steps, alternatives and guarded lifecycle transitions. Projection separates typed topology from selected sequence/state details; omitted semantic facts are not guessed from prose, software paths or Scenario reachability. The reader labels the selected source meaning and its execution limits. This is an observed MOD-004 contribution; collaborating capture/interpretation and package qualification remain separately owned.","gaps":["Demonstrate topology without order/concurrency and source-authorized behavioral detail under the admitted customer profile; unavailable or unsupported detail must remain explicit."],"key":"C3","state":"partial"},{"evidence":[{"limitations":["Accountable source inspection of repository implementation; check names below identify relevant assertions, not an automatic full-criterion pass."],"source":{"change":"2026-10-04-system-requirements-view-design","id":"criterion-assessment-implementation","identity":"sha256:f4223bb2644ad82b0ae43bf7dc6938d5c87604cddcd93fbc49b6e4cbb8b7b65e","kind":"evidence"},"subjects":[{"identity":"sha256:5c7447a3241ef95ea4c3e8444517006e1faf4b30e0306cace0803b5165725932","path":"scripts/lib/rem_architecture_browser.py"},{"identity":"sha256:8d5e4e7cee2dd6280d2127fe86442e1d43f83d9fb7826e902d30a7bc4e890cfa","path":"scripts/lib/rem_architecture_model.py"},{"identity":"sha256:88ccf64b75ac66b2ca6a64a6711667b724fb5a5a31f699d97760712f076ab964","path":"scripts/lib/rem_authored_views.py"},{"identity":"sha256:78e1ed7cfb328736008755d11c044ac318487d6464c3340e5b413eb4f5d0a934","path":"scripts/resources/rem-architecture-browser/viewer.js"},{"identity":"sha256:586ed3d8faea1d8ed6133f9f67d3592594bec6c9d809955a704b22c185a3b9ce","path":"tests/engineering/validation/architecture_browser_tests.py"},{"identity":"sha256:78178721aa41b5967600b8f9848ccbabb157a0588b48da48b0e1919f3e3c7ed3","path":"tests/engineering/validation/architecture_browser_ui_checks.cjs"},{"identity":"sha256:0ca36cdcd69c7204aeb53a1d0f46aeab1fc54dd96f8262883a6f6fa7c2955e86","path":"tests/engineering/validation/architecture_view_tests.py"}],"summary":"Authored-topic identity and route include owner, view, qualification, kind and local ID. Exact document, registration and selected-source digests accompany topics. The reader distinguishes Design/proposed from observed sources and refuses a route with the wrong qualification; generic facets retain proposed, observed and deferred content separately."}],"explanation":"Authored-topic identity and route include owner, view, qualification, kind and local ID. Exact document, registration and selected-source digests accompany topics. The reader distinguishes Design/proposed from observed sources and refuses a route with the wrong qualification; generic facets retain proposed, observed and deferred content separately. This is an observed MOD-004 contribution; collaborating capture/interpretation and package qualification remain separately owned.","gaps":["Carry the independently observed repository same-name proposed/observed separation through the customer selected-state boundary, including overview listing and complete source association. The fresh copied-page contrast closes the corresponding repository evidence gap."],"key":"C4","state":"partial"},{"evidence":[{"limitations":["Accountable source inspection of repository implementation; check names below identify relevant assertions, not an automatic full-criterion pass."],"source":{"change":"2026-10-04-system-requirements-view-design","id":"criterion-assessment-implementation","identity":"sha256:f4223bb2644ad82b0ae43bf7dc6938d5c87604cddcd93fbc49b6e4cbb8b7b65e","kind":"evidence"},"subjects":[{"identity":"sha256:5c7447a3241ef95ea4c3e8444517006e1faf4b30e0306cace0803b5165725932","path":"scripts/lib/rem_architecture_browser.py"},{"identity":"sha256:8d5e4e7cee2dd6280d2127fe86442e1d43f83d9fb7826e902d30a7bc4e890cfa","path":"scripts/lib/rem_architecture_model.py"},{"identity":"sha256:82ee7f6c8af02b1b0d51700066e28787c02a3d4be2f4f27eaa888d899e07643f","path":"scripts/lib/rem_architecture_scenario_diagrams.py"},{"identity":"sha256:10edca5c3931ccac04609d523a0345d51973b83d8c67c6de28fcf058f27d201a","path":"scripts/lib/rem_architecture_scenarios.py"},{"identity":"sha256:78e1ed7cfb328736008755d11c044ac318487d6464c3340e5b413eb4f5d0a934","path":"scripts/resources/rem-architecture-browser/viewer.js"},{"identity":"sha256:586ed3d8faea1d8ed6133f9f67d3592594bec6c9d809955a704b22c185a3b9ce","path":"tests/engineering/validation/architecture_browser_tests.py"},{"identity":"sha256:78178721aa41b5967600b8f9848ccbabb157a0588b48da48b0e1919f3e3c7ed3","path":"tests/engineering/validation/architecture_browser_ui_checks.cjs"},{"identity":"sha256:0ca36cdcd69c7204aeb53a1d0f46aeab1fc54dd96f8262883a6f6fa7c2955e86","path":"tests/engineering/validation/architecture_view_tests.py"}],"summary":"Scenario projection preserves source-defined expected, alternative and failure outcomes and exact selected obligation text. Accountable allocations remain distinct from provider context. The reader preserves black-box meaning and warns that reachability, rendering and related test groups do not establish coverage, approval or satisfaction."}],"explanation":"Scenario projection preserves source-defined expected, alternative and failure outcomes and exact selected obligation text. Accountable allocations remain distinct from provider context. The reader preserves black-box meaning and warns that reachability, rendering and related test groups do not establish coverage, approval or satisfaction. This is an observed MOD-004 contribution; collaborating capture/interpretation and package qualification remain separately owned.","gaps":["Demonstrate the same preservation for selected customer Scenarios without requiring the RigorLoop-specific reading profiles; inspect unknown participation and unprofiled outcomes as well as the declared paths."],"key":"C5","state":"partial"},{"evidence":[{"limitations":["Accountable source inspection of repository implementation; check names below identify relevant assertions, not an automatic full-criterion pass."],"source":{"change":"2026-10-04-system-requirements-view-design","id":"criterion-assessment-implementation","identity":"sha256:f4223bb2644ad82b0ae43bf7dc6938d5c87604cddcd93fbc49b6e4cbb8b7b65e","kind":"evidence"},"subjects":[{"identity":"sha256:5c7447a3241ef95ea4c3e8444517006e1faf4b30e0306cace0803b5165725932","path":"scripts/lib/rem_architecture_browser.py"},{"identity":"sha256:8d5e4e7cee2dd6280d2127fe86442e1d43f83d9fb7826e902d30a7bc4e890cfa","path":"scripts/lib/rem_architecture_model.py"},{"identity":"sha256:10edca5c3931ccac04609d523a0345d51973b83d8c67c6de28fcf058f27d201a","path":"scripts/lib/rem_architecture_scenarios.py"},{"identity":"sha256:6ad804d6e7c54e1f18c09f4d38288eacd4f2ef901ea3dd9dceefa1156f09b745","path":"scripts/lib/rem_browser_assessments.py"},{"identity":"sha256:a0b9939b83431dc400d282973b37beced5e4d932bb74bdbe838e76270732f402","path":"scripts/render-rem-architecture-browser.py"},{"identity":"sha256:78e1ed7cfb328736008755d11c044ac318487d6464c3340e5b413eb4f5d0a934","path":"scripts/resources/rem-architecture-browser/viewer.js"},{"identity":"sha256:02918407413c291a591caf6bfdae73d2a0597c32ed058a40e97f4ad6530e13c3","path":"tests/engineering/validation/architecture_assessment_ui_checks.cjs"},{"identity":"sha256:586ed3d8faea1d8ed6133f9f67d3592594bec6c9d809955a704b22c185a3b9ce","path":"tests/engineering/validation/architecture_browser_tests.py"},{"identity":"sha256:78178721aa41b5967600b8f9848ccbabb157a0588b48da48b0e1919f3e3c7ed3","path":"tests/engineering/validation/architecture_browser_ui_checks.cjs"},{"identity":"sha256:0ca36cdcd69c7204aeb53a1d0f46aeab1fc54dd96f8262883a6f6fa7c2955e86","path":"tests/engineering/validation/architecture_view_tests.py"}],"summary":"Missing optional realization shows a visible empty state; unresolved required selectors reject before compilation/publication. Scenario outcomes keep unselected detail gaps. Delivery accounts preserve absence, criterion gaps and stale/conflicting support independently from Design; a successful rendering does not supply a complete-design or requirement-satisfaction judgment."}],"explanation":"Missing optional realization shows a visible empty state; unresolved required selectors reject before compilation/publication. Scenario outcomes keep unselected detail gaps. Delivery accounts preserve absence, criterion gaps and stale/conflicting support independently from Design; a successful rendering does not supply a complete-design or requirement-satisfaction judgment. This is an observed MOD-004 contribution; collaborating capture/interpretation and package qualification remain separately owned.","gaps":["Qualify missing required rationale separately from missing optional history/detail in the customer artifact, preserving useful known content and explicit incomplete scope across view changes."],"key":"C6","state":"partial"}],"design_support":[],"identity":"sha256:4b147028d7df40264213fdb074dd8df6c9a3006beb93b278c96e3ed6f5902c18","limitations":["Observed implementation is the repository Python/D2 browser; the designed customer engine and source-profile boundary remain proposed.","This implementation assessment is distinct from requirement Verification and does not infer satisfaction from Design coverage, links or test counts."],"membership":null,"nonreliance":[],"reported_at":"2026-10-06T13:16:59Z","source":{"change":"2026-10-04-system-requirements-view-design","id":"criterion-assessment-implementation","identity":"sha256:f4223bb2644ad82b0ae43bf7dc6938d5c87604cddcd93fbc49b6e4cbb8b7b65e","kind":"evidence"},"state":"partial","subjects":[{"identity":"sha256:705977004fbc8037699b3af0210641e5ebef9b8404abe990e9e2bc55d2520e5f","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-016-engineering-model-management/modules/MOD-004-engineering-context-and-traceability/README.md"},{"identity":"sha256:ee1303ac9c01e11d53b3d6af2c47fc915d37488f8db490d9de524c106bc7f9f3","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-016-engineering-model-management/modules/MOD-004-engineering-context-and-traceability/requirement-delivery-format.md"},{"identity":"sha256:98c94da392584be5a65a45b09120621d96fa4d26e157ae0e7294414d3b64ddb3","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-016-engineering-model-management/modules/MOD-004-engineering-context-and-traceability/requirement-tree.md"},{"identity":"sha256:915876f00dba078b8ffefdcd17f951997f444485c5545548d679d2f2d1d2f477","path":"design/support/requirement-delivery-v2.schema.json"},{"identity":"sha256:5c7447a3241ef95ea4c3e8444517006e1faf4b30e