no inherited parent satisfaction. Required-reference rejection and optional absence remain distinct mechanisms rather than fabricated detail."}],"explanation":"Positive repository observations support a bounded contribution; complete MOD-004 criterion contribution in its declared customer scope is not established. Observe customer cases distinguishing missing required rationale from unavailable optional history/detail, plus invalid/incomplete selection and view changes. Known content must remain useful with its precise limitation; current empty-state/assessment tests do not establish the entire required explanatory-content classification.","gaps":["Observe customer cases distinguishing missing required rationale from unavailable optional history/detail, plus invalid/incomplete selection and view changes. Known content must remain useful with its precise limitation; current empty-state/assessment tests do not establish the entire required explanatory-content classification."],"key":"C6","state":"not-assessed"}],"design_support":[],"identity":"sha256:f6ebc9cbcf45e128e46fad76316460c69121b60daea936574a839f56a780b086","limitations":["Actual full-scope assessment is inconclusive, represented as Not assessed. This is an assessed insufficiency of complete acceptance proof, not absence of any engineering inspection, not an observed failure and not a stale prior positive result.","The owned target is customer-project/profile behavior; observed implementation and executed proof here are the repository Python/D2 projection and Chromium151/Linux reader. MOD004 README and realization facets explicitly retain the customer Node/Rust engine and public boundary as proposed.","Each criterion has positive bounded repository observations; none is marked full-scope Passed because the declared customer-context proof is missing. No complete requirement Verification is inferred from test totals, Design Covered, the earlier scoped extension Verify, or the parent/child relationship.","The same-name contrast is a private synthetic injected reader case with preserved fixture bytes. It does not assert that an authored proposed diagram is an observed runtime fact or test the full customer source admission/compiler chain.","Required rationale versus optional history remains a specific residual content-classification proof obligation. A passing empty view or invalid reference rejection alone is not substituted for that contrast.","Root full local CI reconciliation is running independently at assessment preparation time; this report neither asserts its outcome nor reuses the earlier preflight limitation as a current failure. Its eventual result cannot close the customer semantic proof gaps automatically."],"membership":null,"nonreliance":[],"reported_at":"2026-10-06T13:21:58Z","source":{"change":"2026-10-04-system-requirements-view-design","id":"criterion-assessment-ar046","identity":"sha256:14d3f8df5b4a8c9289b9f306f00abbd0890dc2f3f55b0a9955f46b27d9be55fc","kind":"verification"},"state":"not-assessed","subjects":[{"identity":"sha256:8d5e4e7cee2dd6280d2127fe86442e1d43f83d9fb7826e902d30a7bc4e890cfa","path":"scripts/lib/rem_architecture_model.py"},{"identity":"sha256:5c7447a3241ef95ea4c3e8444517006e1faf4b30e0306cace0803b5165725932","path":"scripts/lib/rem_architecture_browser.py"},{"identity":"sha256:2ec4643a7735f85cd67b670a34c7aa52e71352ea5c19101e53e0ac5a48358e77","path":"scripts/lib/rem_architecture_realization_diagrams.py"},{"identity":"sha256:10edca5c3931ccac04609d523a0345d51973b83d8c67c6de28fcf058f27d201a","path":"scripts/lib/rem_architecture_scenarios.py"},{"identity":"sha256:82ee7f6c8af02b1b0d51700066e28787c02a3d4be2f4f27eaa888d899e07643f","path":"scripts/lib/rem_architecture_scenario_diagrams.py"},{"identity":"sha256:88ccf64b75ac66b2ca6a64a6711667b724fb5a5a31f699d97760712f076ab964","path":"scripts/lib/rem_authored_views.py"},{"identity":"sha256:6ad804d6e7c54e1f18c09f4d38288eacd4f2ef901ea3dd9dceefa1156f09b745","path":"scripts/lib/rem_browser_assessments.py"},{"identity":"sha256:a0b9939b83431dc400d282973b37beced5e4d932bb74bdbe838e76270732f402","path":"scripts/render-rem-architecture-browser.py"},{"identity":"sha256:78e1ed7cfb328736008755d11c044ac318487d6464c3340e5b413eb4f5d0a934","path":"scripts/resources/rem-architecture-browser/viewer.js"},{"identity":"sha256:fff142393fc3f195ee04860df52f2a300275226a239273ca8e3594e7914806f8","path":"scripts/resources/rem-architecture-browser/viewer.css"},{"identity":"sha256:0ca36cdcd69c7204aeb53a1d0f46aeab1fc54dd96f8262883a6f6fa7c2955e86","path":"tests/engineering/validation/architecture_view_tests.py"},{"identity":"sha256:586ed3d8faea1d8ed6133f9f67d3592594bec6c9d809955a704b22c185a3b9ce","path":"tests/engineering/validation/architecture_browser_tests.py"},{"identity":"sha256:78178721aa41b5967600b8f9848ccbabb157a0588b48da48b0e1919f3e3c7ed3","path":"tests/engineering/validation/architecture_browser_ui_checks.cjs"},{"identity":"sha256:02918407413c291a591caf6bfdae73d2a0597c32ed058a40e97f4ad6530e13c3","path":"tests/engineering/validation/architecture_assessment_ui_checks.cjs"},{"identity":"sha256:705977004fbc8037699b3af0210641e5ebef9b8404abe990e9e2bc55d2520e5f","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-016-engineering-model-management/modules/MOD-004-engineering-context-and-traceability/README.md"}],"summary":"All six criteria were independently assessed. Existing repository behavior and bounded checks provide positive contributions for C1-C6, but complete declared MOD-004 customer-browser contribution is not verified. Full-scope outcome is inconclusive / Not assessed; no criterion failure is observed."}},{"definition":{"content":"{\n  \"id\": \"SR-085\",\n  \"type\": \"system-requirement\",\n  \"title\": \"Preserve engineering meaning across architecture views\",\n  \"status\": \"draft\",\n  \"statement\": \"The system shall present the five architecture views and their selected details as attributable projections of the selected model, preserving ownership, relationship meaning, qualification and completeness limits.\",\n  \"analysis\": {\n    \"method\": \"5W2H\",\n    \"what\": {\n      \"problem\": \"A view may misrepresent facts or hide incomplete interpretation.\",\n      \"desired_outcome\": \"present the five architecture views and their selected details as attributable projections of the selected model, preserving ownership, relationship meaning, qualification and completeness limits.\"\n    },\n    \"why\": {\n      \"rationale\": \"Customer use needs attributable, portable views and truthful boundaries beyond repository-local demonstration.\"\n    },\n    \"who\": {\n      \"stakeholders\": [\n        \"Customer model authors and readers\",\n        \"Product maintainers and reviewers\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"when\": {\n      \"conditions\": [\n        \"When generating, reading or qualifying the selected architecture browser capability.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"where\": {\n      \"contexts\": [\n        \"One selected customer project/state and explicitly selected output; declared product generation and reading environments.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"how\": {\n      \"approach\": \"Assess the stated observable outcomes against explicit supported profiles, selected source identity and actual artifacts; preserve ownership and diagnose unavailable or incomplete results.\"\n    },\n    \"how_much\": {\n      \"scope\": \"Read-only local generation and portable snapshot reading. No live editor, hosted-service requirement, cross-project aggregation, automatic publication or invented performance target. Detailed realization and platform support are downstream design decisions.\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n    \"Readers can navigate each available view from an overview to relevant definitions, relationships and applicable rationale, using readable labels and keyboard-accessible navigation.\",\n    \"Logical ownership and containment remain distinct from execution and deployment; a shared source file does not merge logical responsibilities.\",\n    \"Process topology does not imply execution order or concurrency. Selected activity, interaction and lifecycle details appear only where authoritative semantics establish them.\",\n    \"Proposed and observed facts remain distinguishable in overviews and details, even when names are identical; each detail exposes its selected-state source basis.\",\n    \"Scenario navigation retains stakeholder meaning and identified architecture participation without turning reachability or rendering into coverage, approval or satisfaction.\",\n    \"Missing required explanation and incomplete selections remain explicit; absent details are not fabricated and view success does not establish a complete design.\"\n  ],\n  \"assumptions\": [],\n  \"constraints\": [],\n  \"confirms\": [\n    \"FUNC-007\",\n    \"FUNC-009\",\n    \"FUNC-080\",\n    \"FUNC-081\"\n  ],\n  \"constrains\": [\n    \"FEAT-022\"\n  ],\n  \"sources\": [\n    {\n      \"source\": \"SRC-CUSTOMER-BROWSER-REQUIREMENTS\",\n      \"locator\": \"SR-085\",\n      \"basis\": \"User-requested reusable customer architecture browser; requirement-level author analysis. Current records remain draft; no implemented, published or independently approved behavior is claimed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"SRC-CUSTOMER-BROWSER-DESIGN\",\n      \"locator\": \"SR-085\",\n      \"basis\": \"System and Architecture Design from SR-084\\u2013088 and refined SR-060; proposed responsibility, contract and realization only. No implementation, platform qualification or product availability is established.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n","identity":"sha256:bd4a159c76fca8c27594707ebd2d95bd43a07a76b27b0e06f022b823beaa9f94","path":"design/requirements/IR-002-trace-engineering-obligations-and-responsibilities/SR-085-preserve-engineering-meaning-across-architecture-views/sr.json"},"implementation":{"actor":"root / verify (implementation-source assessment)","applicability":{"explanation":"Exact material sources inspected and compared. Actual assessor scope, observations and residual customer-context gaps retained; no full-scope positive conclusion.","state":"current"},"child_support":[],"concerns":[],"criteria":[{"evidence":[{"limitations":["Accountable source inspection of repository implementation; check names below identify relevant assertions, not an automatic full-criterion pass."],"source":{"change":"2026-10-04-system-requirements-view-design","id":"criterion-assessment-implementation","identity":"sha256:f4223bb2644ad82b0ae43bf7dc6938d5c87604cddcd93fbc49b6e4cbb8b7b65e","kind":"evidence"},"subjects":[{"identity":"sha256:5c7447a3241ef95ea4c3e8444517006e1faf4b30e0306cace0803b5165725932","path":"scripts/lib/rem_architecture_browser.py"},{"identity":"sha256:8d5e4e7cee2dd6280d2127fe86442e1d43f83d9fb7826e902d30a7bc4e890cfa","path":"scripts/lib/rem_architecture_model.py"},{"identity":"sha256:88ccf64b75ac66b2ca6a64a6711667b724fb5a5a31f699d97760712f076ab964","path":"scripts/lib/rem_authored_views.py"},{"identity":"sha256:a0b9939b83431dc400d282973b37beced5e4d932bb74bdbe838e76270732f402","path":"scripts/render-rem-architecture-browser.py"},{"identity":"sha256:fff142393fc3f195ee04860df52f2a300275226a239273ca8e3594e7914806f8","path":"scripts/resources/rem-architecture-browser/viewer.css"},{"identity":"sha256:78e1ed7cfb328736008755d11c044ac318487d6464c3340e5b413eb4f5d0a934","path":"scripts/resources/rem-architecture-browser/viewer.js"},{"identity":"sha256:586ed3d8faea1d8ed6133f9f67d3592594bec6c9d809955a704b22c185a3b9ce","path":"tests/engineering/validation/architecture_browser_tests.py"},{"identity":"sha256:78178721aa41b5967600b8f9848ccbabb157a0588b48da48b0e1919f3e3c7ed3","path":"tests/engineering/validation/architecture_browser_ui_checks.cjs"},{"identity":"sha256:0ca36cdcd69c7204aeb53a1d0f46aeab1fc54dd96f8262883a6f6fa7c2955e86","path":"tests/engineering/validation/architecture_view_tests.py"}],"summary":"The repository renderer embeds source records, typed relationships and qualified topics; the reader links system and Module overviews to definitions, relationships, source text and rationale. Native links, buttons and focus handling support keyboard navigation, including the expandable requirement tree."}],"explanation":"The repository renderer embeds source records, typed relationships and qualified topics; the reader links system and Module overviews to definitions, relationships, source text and rationale. Native links, buttons and focus handling support keyboard navigation, including the expandable requirement tree. This is direct reference-browser behavior supporting the system criterion; it does not establish the end-to-end customer system outcome.","gaps":["Demonstrate overview-to-definition/relationship/required-rationale navigation across all available views on the selected customer model, with declared keyboard/readability support and explicit unavailable rationale."],"key":"C1","state":"partial"},{"evidence":[{"limitations":["Accountable source inspection of repository implementation; check names below identify relevant assertions, not an automatic full-criterion pass."],"source":{"change":"2026-10-04-system-requirements-view-design","id":"criterion-assessment-implementation","identity":"sha256:f4223bb2644ad82b0ae43bf7dc6938d5c87604cddcd93fbc49b6e4cbb8b7b65e","kind":"evidence"},"subjects":[{"identity":"sha256:5c7447a3241ef95ea4c3e8444517006e1faf4b30e0306cace0803b5165725932","path":"scripts/lib/rem_architecture_browser.py"},{"identity":"sha256:8d5e4e7cee2dd6280d2127fe86442e1d43f83d9fb7826e902d30a7bc4e890cfa","path":"scripts/lib/rem_architecture_model.py"},{"identity":"sha256:4ef2966248278de32fa8e138c270333df889f7f39bfef80a5232a3aa5cea1740","path":"scripts/lib/rem_architecture_physical.py"},{"identity":"sha256:2ec4643a7735f85cd67b670a34c7aa52e71352ea5c19101e53e0ac5a48358e77","path":"scripts/lib/rem_architecture_realization_diagrams.py"},{"identity":"sha256:78e1ed7cfb328736008755d11c044ac318487d6464c3340e5b413eb4f5d0a934","path":"scripts/resources/rem-architecture-browser/viewer.js"},{"identity":"sha256:586ed3d8faea1d8ed6133f9f67d3592594bec6c9d809955a704b22c185a3b9ce","path":"tests/engineering/validation/architecture_browser_tests.py"},{"identity":"sha256:78178721aa41b5967600b8f9848ccbabb157a0588b48da48b0e1919f3e3c7ed3","path":"tests/engineering/validation/architecture_browser_ui_checks.cjs"},{"identity":"sha256:0ca36cdcd69c7204aeb53a1d0f46aeab1fc54dd96f8262883a6f6fa7c2955e86","path":"tests/engineering/validation/architecture_view_tests.py"}],"summary":"build_model separates direct Function/AR allocation from subtree summaries and exact Interface provider from exposure. Development diagrams group source mappings under each accountable owner; typed execution and placement projections use separate source facts. Shared source paths therefore do not define or merge logical ownership."}],"explanation":"build_model separates direct Function/AR allocation from subtree summaries and exact Interface provider from exposure. Development diagrams group source mappings under each accountable owner; typed execution and placement projections use separate source facts. Shared source paths therefore do not define or merge logical ownership. This is direct reference-browser behavior supporting the system criterion; it does not establish the end-to-end customer system outcome.","gaps":["Carry the proven repository shared-source ownership distinction through the admitted customer capture, interpretation, projection and artifact boundary; inspect overview and details with differing runtime/placement facts."],"key":"C2","state":"partial"},{"evidence":[{"limitations":["Accountable source inspection of repository implementation; check names below identify relevant assertions, not an automatic full-criterion pass."],"source":{"change":"2026-10-04-system-requirements-view-design","id":"criterion-assessment-implementation","identity":"sha256:f4223bb2644ad82b0ae43bf7dc6938d5c87604cddcd93fbc49b6e4cbb8b7b65e","kind":"evidence"},"subjects":[{"id