chanisms rather than fabricated detail."}],"explanation":"Positive repository observations support a bounded contribution; complete system criterion is not established. Observe customer cases distinguishing missing required rationale from unavailable optional history/detail, plus invalid/incomplete selection and view changes. Known content must remain useful with its precise limitation; current empty-state/assessment tests do not establish the entire required explanatory-content classification.","gaps":["Observe customer cases distinguishing missing required rationale from unavailable optional history/detail, plus invalid/incomplete selection and view changes. Known content must remain useful with its precise limitation; current empty-state/assessment tests do not establish the entire required explanatory-content classification."],"key":"C6","state":"not-assessed"}],"design_support":[],"identity":"sha256:15461b673edff65c1bba3fedefb0f00e992dbfb211267482a531bcc7c6cb41f5","limitations":["Actual full-scope assessment is inconclusive, represented as Not assessed. This is an assessed insufficiency of complete acceptance proof, not absence of any engineering inspection, not an observed failure and not a stale prior positive result.","The owned target is customer-project/profile behavior; observed implementation and executed proof here are the repository Python/D2 projection and Chromium151/Linux reader. MOD004 README and realization facets explicitly retain the customer Node/Rust engine and public boundary as proposed.","Each criterion has positive bounded repository observations; none is marked full-scope Passed because the declared customer-context proof is missing. No complete requirement Verification is inferred from test totals, Design Covered, the earlier scoped extension Verify, or the parent/child relationship.","The same-name contrast is a private synthetic injected reader case with preserved fixture bytes. It does not assert that an authored proposed diagram is an observed runtime fact or test the full customer source admission/compiler chain.","Required rationale versus optional history remains a specific residual content-classification proof obligation. A passing empty view or invalid reference rejection alone is not substituted for that contrast.","Root full local CI reconciliation is running independently at assessment preparation time; this report neither asserts its outcome nor reuses the earlier preflight limitation as a current failure. Its eventual result cannot close the customer semantic proof gaps automatically."],"membership":null,"nonreliance":[],"reported_at":"2026-10-06T13:21:58Z","source":{"change":"2026-10-04-system-requirements-view-design","id":"criterion-assessment-sr085","identity":"sha256:96f436c833ec3ecf0eabf62bd44c1cb47e3c29d882ef8ad8acb6ba6f2bde37fa","kind":"verification"},"state":"not-assessed","subjects":[{"identity":"sha256:8d5e4e7cee2dd6280d2127fe86442e1d43f83d9fb7826e902d30a7bc4e890cfa","path":"scripts/lib/rem_architecture_model.py"},{"identity":"sha256:5c7447a3241ef95ea4c3e8444517006e1faf4b30e0306cace0803b5165725932","path":"scripts/lib/rem_architecture_browser.py"},{"identity":"sha256:2ec4643a7735f85cd67b670a34c7aa52e71352ea5c19101e53e0ac5a48358e77","path":"scripts/lib/rem_architecture_realization_diagrams.py"},{"identity":"sha256:10edca5c3931ccac04609d523a0345d51973b83d8c67c6de28fcf058f27d201a","path":"scripts/lib/rem_architecture_scenarios.py"},{"identity":"sha256:82ee7f6c8af02b1b0d51700066e28787c02a3d4be2f4f27eaa888d899e07643f","path":"scripts/lib/rem_architecture_scenario_diagrams.py"},{"identity":"sha256:88ccf64b75ac66b2ca6a64a6711667b724fb5a5a31f699d97760712f076ab964","path":"scripts/lib/rem_authored_views.py"},{"identity":"sha256:6ad804d6e7c54e1f18c09f4d38288eacd4f2ef901ea3dd9dceefa1156f09b745","path":"scripts/lib/rem_browser_assessments.py"},{"identity":"sha256:a0b9939b83431dc400d282973b37beced5e4d932bb74bdbe838e76270732f402","path":"scripts/render-rem-architecture-browser.py"},{"identity":"sha256:78e1ed7cfb328736008755d11c044ac318487d6464c3340e5b413eb4f5d0a934","path":"scripts/resources/rem-architecture-browser/viewer.js"},{"identity":"sha256:fff142393fc3f195ee04860df52f2a300275226a239273ca8e3594e7914806f8","path":"scripts/resources/rem-architecture-browser/viewer.css"},{"identity":"sha256:0ca36cdcd69c7204aeb53a1d0f46aeab1fc54dd96f8262883a6f6fa7c2955e86","path":"tests/engineering/validation/architecture_view_tests.py"},{"identity":"sha256:586ed3d8faea1d8ed6133f9f67d3592594bec6c9d809955a704b22c185a3b9ce","path":"tests/engineering/validation/architecture_browser_tests.py"},{"identity":"sha256:78178721aa41b5967600b8f9848ccbabb157a0588b48da48b0e1919f3e3c7ed3","path":"tests/engineering/validation/architecture_browser_ui_checks.cjs"},{"identity":"sha256:02918407413c291a591caf6bfdae73d2a0597c32ed058a40e97f4ad6530e13c3","path":"tests/engineering/validation/architecture_assessment_ui_checks.cjs"},{"identity":"sha256:705977004fbc8037699b3af0210641e5ebef9b8404abe990e9e2bc55d2520e5f","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-016-engineering-model-management/modules/MOD-004-engineering-context-and-traceability/README.md"}],"summary":"All six criteria were independently assessed. Existing repository behavior and bounded checks provide positive contributions for C1-C6, but complete system customer-context acceptance is not verified. Full-scope outcome is inconclusive / Not assessed; no criterion failure is observed."}},{"definition":{"content":"{\n  \"id\": \"SR-050\",\n  \"type\": \"system-requirement\",\n  \"title\": \"Expose distinct published engineering capabilities\",\n  \"status\": \"draft\",\n  \"sources\": [\n    {\n      \"source\": \"SRC-PUBLISHED-SKILLS\",\n      \"locator\": \"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-012-published-engineering-capability-guidance/capability-contract.md#SKL-SR-02\",\n      \"basis\": \"Derives the stated common Skills-product obligation while preserving the cited clause population and retained specialist or package-owner detail; this draft is not source retirement or runtime adoption.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"SRC-PUBLISHED-SKILLS\",\n      \"locator\": \"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-012-published-engineering-capability-guidance/capability-contract.md#SKL-SR-03\",\n      \"basis\": \"Derives the stated common Skills-product obligation while preserving the cited clause population and retained specialist or package-owner detail; this draft is not source retirement or runtime adoption.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"SRC-PUBLISHED-SKILLS\",\n      \"locator\": \"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-012-published-engineering-capability-guidance/capability-contract.md#SKL-SR-24\",\n      \"basis\": \"Derives the stated common Skills-product obligation while preserving the cited clause population and retained specialist or package-owner detail; this draft is not source retirement or runtime adoption.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"SRC-PUBLISHED-SKILLS\",\n      \"locator\": \"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-012-published-engineering-capability-guidance/capability-contract.md#SKL-SR-35\",\n      \"basis\": \"Derives the stated common Skills-product obligation while preserving the cited clause population and retained specialist or package-owner detail; this draft is not source retirement or runtime adoption.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"statement\": \"The system shall describe each published engineering capability with its purpose, invocation triggers, relevant exclusions, and behavioral owner so a participant can select work suited to the requested outcome before entering its detailed procedure.\",\n  \"analysis\": {\n    \"method\": \"5W2H\",\n    \"what\": {\n      \"problem\": \"Similar capability names can cause a participant to choose review for authoring, implementation for an unsettled design, or factual research for an unresolved direction.\",\n      \"desired_outcome\": \"The participant can distinguish supported capabilities and their relevant near misses from their public descriptions.\"\n    },\n    \"why\": {\n      \"rationale\": \"Selection must expose actual responsibility and side effects before work begins.\"\n    },\n    \"who\": {\n      \"stakeholders\": [\n        \"Participants invoking published engineering capabilities\",\n        \"Project decision owners and reviewers\",\n        \"Published guidance maintainers\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"when\": {\n      \"conditions\": [\n        \"When discovering a capability or comparing neighboring capabilities for a requested task.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"where\": {\n      \"contexts\": [\n        \"The selected capability path in the participant's project context.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"how\": {\n      \"approach\": \"Present the current public name, purpose, triggers, important exclusions, specialist owner, and local handoff without requiring internal body headings or adapter-only metadata to make selection understandable.\"\n    },\n    \"how_much\": {\n      \"scope\": \"All currently published capabilities. Preserve the selected metadata and description constraints at their existing owner. Descriptions support selection but do not guarantee deterministic agent routing.\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n    \"A participant can distinguish a request to create an artifact, review it, execute implementation, investigate options, or resolve a factual uncertainty using the applicable capability descriptions.\",\n    \"Each published capability identifies one current behavioral owner and a justified recurring responsibility; a package folder alone is insufficient justification.\",\n    \"A description exposes important near misses and applicable scope without hidden mutation or handoff duties, historical rollout labels as runtime prerequisites, or synonym-only selection text.\",\n    \"Unsupported or ambiguous task fit is reported with the missing decision or relevant owner rather than silently selecting an unrelated capability.\"\n  ],\n  \"assumptions\": [],\n  \"constraints\": [],\n  \"confirms\": [\n    \"FUNC-050\"\n  ]\n}\n","identity":"sha256:fd554559017ae6310fe77a7b15616391658fb8c502856be1a71b45d167aa234d","path":"design/requirements/IR-009-carry-out-portable-guided-engineering-work-across-the-project-lifecycle/SR-050-expose-distinct-published-engineering-capabilities/sr.json"},"implementation":null,"kind":"system-requirement","outcome_basis":null,"requirement":"SR-050","scope":"Complete requirement remains the assessment basis; observed implementation contribution is limited to the RigorLoop repository reader. Customer-generator and other unobserved obligations remain explicit gaps.","verification":null},{"definition":{"content":"{\n  \"id\": \"IR-002\",\n  \"type\": \"initial-requirement\",\n  \"title\": \"Trace engineering obligations and responsibilities\",\n  \"status\": \"draft\",\n  \"statement\": \"Engineers, architects, and reviewers need to trace how initial needs relate to system obligations, capabilities, logical behavior, architectural responsibilities, realization, and assurance so they can assess consistency and the effects of proposed changes.\",\n  \"analysis\": {\n    \"method\": \"5W2H\",\n    \"what\": {\n      \"problem\": \"Obligations, capabilities, behavior, architecture, and assurance can become disconnected, leaving their relationships and affected responsibilities unclear.\",\n      \"desired_outcome\": \"Participants can follow the engineering relationships needed to identify responsibility, assess consistency, and investigate the effects of a proposed change.\"\n    },\n    \"why\": {\n      \"rationale\": \"Disconnected engineering information makes it difficult to discover affected responsibilities, missing allocations, and unsupported conclusions.\"\n    },\n    \"who\": {\n      \"stakeholders\": [\n        \"Engineers and architects\",\n        \"Reviewers\",\n        \"Maintainers and engineering agents\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"when\": {\n      \"conditions\": [\n        \"Applies when developing the model, reviewing its consistency, investigating a problem, or assessing the impact of a proposed change.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"where\": {\n      \"contexts\": [\n        \"Across requirement parentage and cross-domain engineering relationships within the governed model.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"how\": {\n      \"approach\": \"Use explicit typed relationships with single-parent requirement containment and graph references across domains. Derive inverse views from the authored facts. SR derivation must distinguish relationship integrity, navigation, allocation consistency, and impact assessment. For the initial authoring profile, a traversal selects its starting entities, relationship types, direction, and model state. Required views include requirement ancestors and descendants, forward and reverse responsibility paths, and affected entities reached through the declared relationship scope. Cycles terminate without repeatedly processing the same traversal state. Requested depth or result limits are explicit, and any resource limit, missing reference, interruption, or truncation prevents an unqualified completeness claim. Customer architecture views project this selected-state information into five attributable perspectives and a portable read-only snapshot; canonical relationships remain authored once.\"\n    },\n    \"how_much\": {\n      \"scope\": \"Covers meaningful requirement parentage and typed cross-domain relationships, including forward and reverse understanding. It does not make relationship presence evidence of requirement satisfaction or prescribe a graph database or user interface. The relationship families are described by REM; this initial need does not establish a quantitative performance target. Traversal is confined to the selected project model and baseline; cross-project and cross-baseline continuation are excluded from this initial profile. There is no implicit depth or result-count cutoff and no elapsed-time service target. Full reachability within the requested scope and explicitly limited exploration are distinguishable results. The customer browser adds explicit generation and offline-reading obligations derived under this need; no particular renderer or hosted service is imposed.\",\n      \"scale\": \"Use the single-project model scope and capacity policy defined by IR-001 analysis.how_much.scale; this requirement adds no separately maintained model-size target.\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"assumptions\": [],\n  \"constraints\": [],\n  \"sources\": [\n    {\n      \"source\": \"SRC-REM\",\n      \"locator\": \"Sections 8, 17, 28, 29, 30, and 34\",\n      \"basis\": \"Strict requirement parentage, converging allocations, and typed graph traceability.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"SRC-VISION\",\n      \"locator\": \"What makes this different; Traceable from idea to verified change\",\n      \"basis\": \"Inspectable traceability from intent through realization and proof.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"SRC-SYSTEM\",\n      \"locator\": \"SYS-SR-03\",\n      \"basis\": \"Related existing traceability obligation; its full contract has not been migrated.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"SRC-REM-REFINEMENT\",\n      \"locator\": \"Requirement Analysis: Analyze the initial need; Name the initial requirement\",\n      \"basis\": \"Required 5W2H analysis and a clearer IR name, preserving the existing identity and need statement.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"SRC-QUESTION-RESOLUTION\",\n      \"locator\": \"IR-002\",\n      \"basis\": \"Resolution of the recorded questions for the initial RigorLoop authoring profile under the user's instruction to solve them; the source register preserves the original questions and rationale.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"SRC-COMPLETE-ANALYSIS\",\n      \"locator\": \"IR-002\",\n      \"basis\": \"Complete this existing IR through governed black-box Scenarios, independently assessable SR obligations, and bounded shared Features and Functions. Preserve the need statement and selected scope; all records remain draft, with architectural allocation and implementation assessment deferred.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"SRC-CUSTOMER-BROWSER-REQUIREMENTS\",\n      \"locator\": \"IR-002\",\n      \"basis\": \"User-requested reusable customer architecture browser; requirement-level author analysis. Current records remain draft; no implemented, published or independently approved behavior is claimed.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"confirms\": [\n    \"FEAT-003\",\n    \"SCN-007\",\n    \"SCN-008\",\n    \"SCN-009\",\n    \"SCN-010\",\n    \"FEAT-022\",\n    \"SCN-083\",\n    \"SCN-084\",\n    \"SCN-085\",\n    \"SCN-086\"\n  ]\n}\n","identity":"sha256:0f980f9704b8d15537eb8254db2ee7a73bc77843930bb5c4b32e72a9640d60fc","path":"design/requirements/IR-002-trace-engineering-obligations-and-responsibilities/ir.json"},"implementation":null,"kind":"initial-requirement","outcome_basis":null,"requirement":"IR-002","scope":"Complete requirement remains the assessment basis; observed implementation contribution is limited to the RigorLoop repository reader. Customer-generator and other unobserved obligations remain explicit gaps.","verification":null}],"format_version":2,"resolutions":[]}
